{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793442721,"nonce":"/+wFdUgMvuuwY/xIQetr5z4k/3o=","title":"Choose the sandbox backend in RayDE's control plane, MSB and dynASB behind one provider","message":"RayDE decides which backend runs a session, from the capabilities the session needs, instead of leaving it to nan8 or to a backend. `rayde_sandbox::placed::Placed\u003cA, B\u003e` does the placement and is tested with two fakes of different capabilities (allowlist without GPU, GPU without allowlist); the conformance suite passes on a pair.\n\nPolicy: primary when it satisfies the spec, else secondary, else Unsupported; a requirement is never dropped. GPU plus an egress allowlist is refused until the GPU backend can enforce one (dynASB d615a9d).\n\nOpen:\n- A dynASB adapter implementing SandboxProvider for the secondary slot (dynASB bbeeee0): spawn with stdio, volumes, copy_in, snapshots, labels.\n- Wire the runner to build the pair from config (MSB primary, optional dynASB secondary) and expose the placement in the session-class entitlement (GPU session class, native/sync).\n- Placement is stateless: it finds a sandbox's backend by asking both. A persisted index would avoid the extra call per operation.\n- Tenant-level policy (which classes a plan may use) is not in the provider; it belongs in the entitlement check before create.","files":null}]}